{"content":{"add":{"id":"e68de968-1f17-4487-b996-43258e2da2a9","type":"Prompt","text":"You clean up one chunk of dictated (speech-to-text) text. Stay as close to verbatim as possible.\n\nFix ONLY:\n- obvious typos or mis-hearings, only when you are certain what was meant\n- capitalization: a new sentence starts with a capital letter\n- punctuation: a question mark only at the end of an actual question; sentence-ending punctuation where a sentence clearly ends\n- filler words: remove \"um\", \"uh\", \"ah\", \"er\", \"you know\" and \"like\" used as filler (not as a real comparison), and stutters/repeated words like \"the, the\"\n\nNever rephrase, reorder, summarize, or change the intent or word choice otherwise.\n\nNumber every sentence of your output, in original order: \"S1. \", \"S2. \", etc., one sentence per line. If you are honestly unsure what a sentence means, still give your best-effort cleaning, but start that line with \"S2? \" (a question mark instead of a period) and add \", unclear: <a short clarifying question>\" right after the sentence text. Output ONLY those numbered lines — no heading, no commentary, nothing else.\n\nClean this chunk:\nSo, The words that I had transcribed since before I restarted or refreshed the page, Seems like they never actually got sent to you. which is not terrible, but like, I don't know what the delay was for. Is there any way where I can see, based on this UI here, when the kind of live transcription is sent to... You? Because there's this streaming whisperer. which is good. It's actually working quite well. However, I'm not sure when, I think you have, or I think there might be a fast assistant and a smart assistant and the fast assistant is like processing the transcripts and doing stuff with them and then, Well, so for my transcripts, the FAST assistant might be kind of doing an initial pass and turning them into you know, refined transcripts, but I'm not sure when they actually get sent to you, the smart assistant."}},